iommu: sun50i: rate-limit the page-fault report

sun50i_iommu_report_fault() runs in hard IRQ context with iommu_lock held
and calls dev_err() unconditionally, once per faulting transaction. That is
survivable while the only translated master is the video engine, which
faults rarely and in bursts. It is not survivable for a display master.

A scanout engine re-reads its framebuffer every frame. If it is switched
into translation while it is still fetching from an address that has no
mapping -- which is exactly the state between the IOMMU attaching the
device and the KMS driver programming its first IOVA -- it faults on every
page of every frame, forever, at 60 Hz. On this board that is thousands of
dev_err() calls per second onto a 115200-baud console from inside a
spinlocked interrupt handler, which is a hang, not a log.

Rate-limit the printing only. report_iommu_fault() still runs on every
fault, so anything registered on the domain sees the true rate, and
sun50i_iommu_zap_range() still runs, so the invalidation behaviour is
unchanged. The suppressed-count line that printk_ratelimited emits keeps
the magnitude visible.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c
@@ -932,13 +932,26 @@
 				      unsigned master, phys_addr_t iova,
 				      unsigned prot)
 {
-	dev_err(iommu->dev, "Page fault for %pad (master %d, dir %s)\n",
-		&iova, master, (prot == IOMMU_FAULT_WRITE) ? "wr" : "rd");
+	/*
+	 * Ratelimited, and it has to be: this runs in hard IRQ context with
+	 * iommu_lock held, once per faulting transaction. A display master
+	 * fetching an unmapped framebuffer faults on every page of every
+	 * frame at 60 Hz, and an unthrottled dev_err() here turns that into
+	 * a console-bound hang rather than a diagnostic.
+	 *
+	 * Only the printing is throttled -- report_iommu_fault() below still
+	 * sees every fault, as does sun50i_iommu_zap_range().
+	 */
+	dev_err_ratelimited(iommu->dev,
+			    "Page fault for %pad (master %d, dir %s)\n",
+			    &iova, master,
+			    (prot == IOMMU_FAULT_WRITE) ? "wr" : "rd");
 
 	if (iommu->domain)
 		report_iommu_fault(iommu->domain, iommu->dev, iova, prot);
 	else
-		dev_err(iommu->dev, "Page fault while iommu not attached to any domain?\n");
+		dev_err_ratelimited(iommu->dev,
+				    "Page fault while iommu not attached to any domain?\n");
 
 	sun50i_iommu_zap_range(iommu, iova, SPAGE_SIZE);
 }
